    <html:strong>What is this website about?</html:strong>
</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
        This website is a collection of my notes and posts on various topics in 
        <html:strong>computer science, mathematics, physics, and programming language theory</html:strong>.
        It is a place where I can organize my thoughts and share my understanding of these topics.
        I hope it can be helpful to others who are interested in these subjects.
    </html:p>
</fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>

    <fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors></fr:authors><fr:title text="
    What is the meaning of &quot;Rabbit Hole&quot;?
">
    <html:strong>What is the meaning of &quot;Rabbit Hole&quot;?</html:strong>
</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter>
    The name of this website &quot;<html:strong>Rabbit Hole</html:strong>&quot; carries a metaphorical significance inspired by Lewis Carroll&apos;s 
    <html:em>Alice&apos;s Adventures in Wonderland</html:em>, 
    meaning to delve into a topic or pursue a line of thought that leads to unexpected or complex places.
    It can refer to getting deeply involved in researching a subject, exploring a particular interest, or going through 
    a series of trees in the forest that leads to a chain of related topics.
</fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>

